WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.615
[MUSIC]

00:00:05.615 --> 00:00:08.832
My grandfather always told me,
don't bet the ranch.

00:00:08.832 --> 00:00:13.299
This is a family entity, there are other
members of your family that rely upon it,

00:00:13.299 --> 00:00:15.643
that's something I take very seriously.

00:00:15.643 --> 00:00:19.784
So that means you have to be making
decisions a little more conservatively,

00:00:19.784 --> 00:00:22.319
you have to be more
patient in your decisions.

00:00:22.319 --> 00:00:27.025
And for him that meant don't bet
the ranch, don't make too big of a play.

00:00:27.025 --> 00:00:30.762
Yet I also think about it today,
I'm 38, and in looking at the next

00:00:30.762 --> 00:00:34.887
25 years plus of my career, and I want to
make sure that I'm in a position and

00:00:34.887 --> 00:00:37.866
leading an organization
that I'm passionate about.

00:00:37.866 --> 00:00:39.656
My name is Ryan O'Melveny Wilson.

00:00:39.656 --> 00:00:43.912
I am the Chief Marketing and
Strategy Officer of Lawry's Restaurants,

00:00:43.912 --> 00:00:44.897
Incorporated.

00:00:44.897 --> 00:00:49.243
I graduated from
the GSB Sloan Class of 2018.

00:00:49.243 --> 00:00:51.224
I'm fourth generation in the business.

00:00:51.224 --> 00:00:54.885
Lawry, the namesake, was Lawrence Frank,
my great grandfather.

00:00:54.885 --> 00:00:59.024
When we opened the restaurant, actually
in the development of the concept,

00:00:59.024 --> 00:01:02.667
my great grandfather wanted to
serve a single entree, that's it.

00:01:02.667 --> 00:01:07.575
He wanted to be one item, and that meal
stayed the same until probably the mid

00:01:07.575 --> 00:01:11.564
80s, when the first change we
incorporated on this menu was

00:01:11.564 --> 00:01:14.728
the inclusion of sour
cream on the baked potato.

00:01:14.728 --> 00:01:16.572
[MUSIC]

00:01:16.572 --> 00:01:19.069
Today we're at
Lawry's The Prime Rib Beverly Hills.

00:01:19.069 --> 00:01:23.575
It's in the midst of a whole reconcepting,
revitalization of business.

00:01:23.575 --> 00:01:28.008
That business opportunity challenge, I've
taken a tremendous amount of learnings

00:01:28.008 --> 00:01:31.331
from my coursework at Stanford
into how to rebuild a business and

00:01:31.331 --> 00:01:33.441
how to make it much more nimble and lean.

00:01:33.441 --> 00:01:36.239
And that's something I'm
really excited about.

00:01:36.239 --> 00:01:39.121
[MUSIC]

00:01:39.121 --> 00:01:42.762
I think, particularly against
the backdrop of Silicon Valley,

00:01:42.762 --> 00:01:45.675
where everyone's expectation
is something new and

00:01:45.675 --> 00:01:50.593
different and a disruptive workplace, a
disruptive company, a disruptive product.

00:01:50.593 --> 00:01:52.513
There's something about coming and
working for

00:01:52.513 --> 00:01:55.238
an established brand that I think
is forgotten in that environment.

00:01:55.238 --> 00:01:56.891
[MUSIC]

00:01:56.891 --> 00:02:01.832
And so when I hear that adage of fail
fast, I think about the idea of constantly

00:02:01.832 --> 00:02:05.037
making evolutions and
progress in a restaurant.

00:02:05.037 --> 00:02:09.625
Every single day we need to be making some
subtle change that is making the dining

00:02:09.625 --> 00:02:10.865
experience better.

00:02:10.865 --> 00:02:13.934
And so fail fast sounds really scary when
you look at it on a big picture, and

00:02:13.934 --> 00:02:15.315
that's something we don't do.

00:02:15.315 --> 00:02:18.584
We take great steps to mitigate
against that big picture risk.

00:02:18.584 --> 00:02:21.925
But on a small scale,
we're always looking to make improvements,

00:02:21.925 --> 00:02:25.149
whether it's a garnish or
a presentation, or trying new salad or

00:02:25.149 --> 00:02:28.449
a slight change in our steps of service or
a new menu presentation.

00:02:28.449 --> 00:02:33.017
I want our organization to always be
willing to make those little changes.

00:02:33.017 --> 00:02:35.228
So one of the great things
about the restaurant business,

00:02:35.228 --> 00:02:37.813
it's one of the few businesses that
has such a tight feedback loop.

00:02:37.813 --> 00:02:40.932
I serve you a salad, I'm going to know
within the first couple of bites if that

00:02:40.932 --> 00:02:43.457
salad is proper temperature,
is served at the proper time,

00:02:43.457 --> 00:02:44.957
that the flavor profile's right.

00:02:44.957 --> 00:02:48.712
I can know very immediately from
your facial reaction, frankly.

00:02:48.712 --> 00:02:50.430
I know that quality is not easy.

00:02:50.430 --> 00:02:54.327
And yet I think quality is ultimately
a differentiator, and I'm not looking for

00:02:54.327 --> 00:02:55.138
the easy fixes.

00:02:55.138 --> 00:02:57.844
I'm looking for
the quality I'm looking for

00:02:57.844 --> 00:03:02.695
things that are going to be attractive to
a specific palate, a specific consumer.

00:03:02.695 --> 00:03:05.671
And to me that's a defining
piece of advice and

00:03:05.671 --> 00:03:09.727
a defining element of how I make
decisions as an entrepreneur.

00:03:09.727 --> 00:03:13.021
And for me, and I want to be in a position
where I'm creating new things, and

00:03:13.021 --> 00:03:14.864
that's speaking to my own motivations.

00:03:14.864 --> 00:03:18.474
And I think it's really important
to express those needs and

00:03:18.474 --> 00:03:23.310
desires rather than just be a slave,
if you will, to what the expectations are.

00:03:23.310 --> 00:03:24.539
I'm passionate about the food.

00:03:24.539 --> 00:03:28.103
And in a family business I think it's okay
to be explicit about what your motivations

00:03:28.103 --> 00:03:29.818
are and what you're passionate about.

00:03:29.818 --> 00:03:33.172
I think in the end that's going to
make you more comfortable and

00:03:33.172 --> 00:03:36.019
more confident and
being in this role for a career.

00:03:36.019 --> 00:03:37.484
I'm not going anywhere, right?

00:03:37.484 --> 00:03:41.994
I'm not looking to jump in 2 years
when the next best offer comes around,

00:03:41.994 --> 00:03:44.707
I'm looking at the next 30 to 40 years.

00:03:44.707 --> 00:03:45.495
[MUSIC]

